{"step_index":1785,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:20:46Z","input_tokens":2222,"cache_read_tokens":200996,"output_tokens":1065,"thinking":"The objective is to create a shell script that launches an identity instance. It will accept instance name, WireGuard public key, and an optional session ID as arguments. The script must generate a concrete instance specification by processing a template, then use the processed specification to create the instance through an API call. A Cozo device image also needs to be created or attached.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# launch-identity.sh: Instantiate a modular 3tchedFS identity container from JSON template.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nusage() {\n    echo \"Usage: $0 <instance-name> <wireguard-pubkey> [session-id]\"\n    echo \"Example: $0 id-1 'Env5zPMmM1Zhypu5/DY/yU4PRYW/4AOEq2KZ4OSc+18=' [uuid]\"\n    exit 1\n}\n\n[[ $# -ge 2 ]] || usage\nINSTANCE_NAME=$1\nWG_PUBKEY=$2\nSESSION_ID=${3:-$(uuidgen | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')}\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/..\" && pwd)\"\nTEMPLATE=\"${REPO_ROOT}/instances/chatbot-template.json\"\nPROFILE_DEF=\"${REPO_ROOT}/profiles/3tched-lungs.json\"\nCOZO_DEV_DIR=\"/var/lib/op-dbus/identity-cozo/devices\"\nIMAGE_PATH=\"${COZO_DEV_DIR}/${INSTANCE_NAME}.img\"\n\n[[ $(id -u) -eq 0 ]] || { echo \"Error: Must be run as root.\" >&2; exit 1; }\n\necho \"==> 1. Ensuring 3tched-lungs profile is registered in Incus...\"\nif ! incus profile show 3tched-lungs >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    incus query -X POST /1.0/profiles -d @\"${PROFILE_DEF}\"\nfi\n\necho \"==> 2. Preparing per-container Cozo & leaf storage image...\"\nif [[ ! -f \"${IMAGE_PATH}\" ]]; then\n    \"${REPO_ROOT}/storage/make-cozo-device.sh\" \"${IMAGE_PATH}\" 20\nfi\n\necho \"==> 3. Generating instance JSON for ${INSTANCE_NAME} (Session: ${SESSION_ID})...\"\nPAYLOAD=$(sed \\\n    -e \"s|{{INSTANCE_NAME}}|${INSTANCE_NAME}|g\" \\\n    -e \"s|{{DISPLAY_NAME}}|${INSTANCE_NAME}|g\" \\\n    -e \"s|{{SESSION_ID}}|${SESSION_ID}|g\" \\\n    -e \"s|{{WIREGUARD_PUBKEY}}|${WG_PUBKEY}|g\" \\\n    \"${TEMPLATE}\")\n\necho \"==> 4. Creating instance via Incus REST API...\"\nRESPONSE=$(incus query -X POST /1.0/instances -d \"${PAYLOAD}\")\necho \"${RESPONSE}\" | jq -r '.status // \"ok\"'\n\necho \"==> 5. Attaching Cozo disk device to container...\"\nincus config device add \"${INSTANCE_NAME}\" cozo-storage disk \\\n    source=\"${IMAGE_PATH}\" \\\n    path=/dev/cozo-disk\n\necho \"==> 6. Starting container ${INSTANCE_NAME}...\"\nincus start \"${INSTANCE_NAME}\"\n\necho \"==> 7. Initializing storage inside container...\"\n# Partition 1 is the Btrfs leaf sprout; partition 2 is ext4 Cozo store\nincus exec \"${INSTANCE_NAME}\" -- mkdir -p /persist /var/lib/op-dbus\nincus exec \"${INSTANCE_NAME}\" -- mount -t ext4 /dev/cozo-disk2 /var/lib/op-dbus 2>/dev/null || true\nincus exec \"${INSTANCE_NAME}\" -- btrfs device add /dev/cozo-disk1 / 2>/dev/null || true\n\necho \"==> Successfully launched identity container: ${INSTANCE_NAME} (${SESSION_ID})\"\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"/srv/git/3tched-container/scripts/launch-identity.sh"}}]}
